PolicyManagerCancelByOwnerTest
├── When no setup and no attempt was ever recorded
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt carrying the caller and the action.
├── When a setup exists but no attempt was ever recorded
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt carrying the caller and the action.
├── When the last attempt is cancelled or consumed
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt carrying the caller and the action.
├── When no attempt is waiting and the named id is not the last attempt's
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt rather than a wrong id.
├── When an attempt is waiting
│   ├── It should set the attempt to Cancelled and keep the rest of its record.
│   ├── It should emit AttemptCancelled alone with the account as canceller and no places.
│   ├── It should leave the setup and the attempt counter unchanged.
│   └── It should refuse a second cancel with nothing left to cancel.
├── When the named id is not the waiting attempt's id
│   ├── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId carrying the named id and the waiting id.
│   └── It should leave the attempt waiting and the state untouched.
├── When the named id is an earlier attempt's id
│   ├── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId carrying the earlier id and the waiting id.
│   └── It should leave the later attempt waiting.
├── When the action stopped serving the account
│   ├── It should cancel the attempt.
│   └── It should not ask the action.
├── When the attempt's methods report a stop or revert on every call
│   └── It should cancel without reaching any method or pause read.
├── When the attempt carries a setup nonce other than the stored one
│   └── It should cancel it, since the holder's cancel reads no setup nonce.
├── When a new setup already ended the attempt
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and leave the ended record untouched.
├── When a clear already ended the attempt
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and leave the ended record untouched.
└── When an address other than the account calls
    ├── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt carrying that address and the action.
    └── It should leave the account's attempt waiting.
